    "7": {
      "uid": 7,
      "key": [
        "The Unforged",
        "Through the Eyes of a Dragon",
        "Iron Tongue Tian"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [],
      "comment": "Azhdaha: The Unforged and the folk tale",
      "content": "Item text for The Unforged tells of a stone dragon in Liyue as large as the mountains, who slept at Nantianmen; his stirring shook the earth and Rex Lapis came to calm it. The text hints the union of dragons, gods and men did not last. The storyteller Iron Tongue Tian tells a folk version: Rex Lapis carved a dragon from a stone and gave it eyes, and it flew into the clouds.",
